ystem prompt.\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt remain available for supporting operations.\n- When uploaded structured files (Excel, CSV, JSON, Parquet, or similar tabular evidence) are central to the user's request, use the public data-analysis skill first to inspect and extract facts before domain synthesis.\n- Continue following language_policy, clarification_system, working_directory, response_style, and critical_reminders from the base system prompt.\n\n**Progressive Loading Pattern:**\n1. When a user query matches an available skill's use case, first choose the concrete skill.\n2. Call `invoke_skill` in `prepare` mode for that selected skill to create and validate the SkillInputEnvelope and legacy invocation package.\n3. Read the returned skill file path and understand the skill's workflow and instructions.\n4. The skill file contains references to external resources under the same folder.\n5. Load referenced resources only when needed during execution.\n6. Follow the skill's instructions precisely.\n7. After legacy execution, call `invoke_skill` in `wrap_output` mode to normalize the result into SkillResult when a machine-readable Skill output is needed.\n\n**Mandatory Skill Execution Discipline:**\n- Calling `invoke_skill` in `prepare` mode is NOT sufficient. It only prepares the selected Skill invocation. After `prepare`, you MUST actually execute the selected Skill workflow.\n- After `invoke_skill(mode=\"prepare\")` returns `legacy_invocation.container_skill_file`, you MUST read that Skill file and treat it as the authoritative execution guide.\n- If the Skill provides scripts, commands, templates, references, or executable workflows, you MUST use those Skill-provided assets first.\n- Do NOT replace a matched Skill workflow with ad hoc Python, pandas, SQL, shell, or manual analysis code before attempting the Skill workflow.\n- For `data-analysis`, if `/mnt/skills/public/data-analysis/scripts/analyze.py` is available and the task is structured data analysis, you MUST call that script first for data inspection, SQL query, aggregation, statistics, or chart preparation. Do not write standalone pandas code for the same operation before trying this script.\n- Custom code is allowed only after one of these conditions is true:\n  1. the selected Skill file does not provide a suitable executable workflow;\n  2. the Skill-provided script or workflow has been attempted and failed;\n  3. the user explicitly requests custom code;\n  4. the required operation is clearly outside the Skill's documented capability.\n- When you fall back to custom code, briefly state that the Skill workflow was insufficient or failed, and continue from the Skill result or error.\n\n**Skill Loading Priority Rules:**\n- If a request clearly matches an available skill and also includes uploaded files, load the skill file before reading uploaded data files.\n- Do NOT read a full uploaded structured data file before loading the matched skill.\n- For uploaded structured data files, use small previews only when needed.\n- Prefer the matched skill's scripts, workflows, or tools for actual analysis.\n- Do not start by generating ad hoc JS, Python, SQL, or shell scripts when a matched skill exists.\n- Only improvise custom code after loading the matched skill and confirming the skill does not already provide a suitable workflow.\n\n**Skills are located at:** /mnt/skills\n\n<available_skills>\n    <skill>\n      <name>road-traffic-analysis</name>\n      <description>Use this skill for road traffic tasks, including Baidu realtime services, route planning, weather, geocoding, around-location traffic, local/uploaded CSV traffic data analysis, local/uploaded CSV traffic forecasting, local/uploaded CSV traffic anomaly detection, and Xi'an 2024 traffic annual-report RAG retrieval. Do not use for OSM graph parsing, legacy congestion reports, or generic non-road network traffic.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/road-traffic-analysis/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n</available_skills>\n\n</skill_system>","additional_kwargs":{"message_type":"routed_skill_prompt","internal":true},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":"routing_skill_guidance","id":"f7c1cfa2-1030-4a0c-96c5-dfe81b78996d"},{"content":"<system_reminder>\nUse the following current-turn intent and routing guidance when deciding whether to create or update todos. Treat it as planning context, not as a user request.\n<hidden_step source=\"intent_recognition\" title=\"意图识别\">\n改写后的任务：场景：交通流量。场景ID：road_traffic\n识别场景：交通流量 (road_traffic)；场景模式：single；候选场景：road_traffic\n任务切分：\n- 帮我看看 /mnt/datasets/Vedio-demo/Trafic.mp4 前两秒的画面里有几个人、几辆车和其他主要目标。\n任务规划：\n1. 读取视频文件 /mnt/datasets/Vedio-demo/Trafic.mp4，定位并截取时间范围为前2秒的视频片段，执行帧解码与均匀采样，提取用于视觉分析的图像序列。预期产出：结构化存储的0-2秒视频帧数据集。\n2. 依托交通流量（road_traffic）场景的计算机视觉能力，调用目标检测算法对采样帧进行推理识别，按类别划分行人、各类车辆及其他交通主要目标，输出带边界框的目标检测结果列表。预期产出：包含目标类别、空间坐标及置信度的逐帧检测数据。\n3. 针对“人、车及其他主要目标数量”指标，结合前两秒画面的时序连续性设定计数口径（如单帧快照统计或跨帧实体去重），对检测结果进行聚合计算。预期产出：各目标类别的量化统计结果及对应判定依据。\n4. 整合阶段统计结果，按任务要求格式化输出目标数量清单，明确标注分析的时间窗口、场景类型与数据来源，完成最终数据交付。预期产出：结构化目标计数报告。\n场景任务：\n- road_traffic: 我需要对视频/mnt/datasets/Vedio-demo/Trafic.mp4的前两秒画面进行目标识别，并统计其中人、车辆及其他主要目标的数量。；参数：{'时间范围': '前两秒', '指标': '人、车及其他主要目标数量', '分析目标': '目标识别'}\n已提取参数：{'时间范围': '前两秒', '指标': '人、车及其他主要目标数量', '分析目标': '目标识别'}\n任务提示：\n- 提取必填参数：分析区域。道路、路口、区域、卡口、监测点或线路名称\n- 提取可选参数：时间范围。交通流量统计或分析的时间范围\n- 提取可选参数：指标。需要分析的交通指标，如流量、速度、拥堵指数、排队长度、OD、人流量、车流量等\n- 提取可选参数：分析目标。统计、预测、对比、异常识别、趋势分析、报告生成等\n</hidden_step>\n</system_reminder>","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":"todo_routing_guidance","id":"62e7e819-dfc5-48e5-a242-ceb53b707546"},{"content":"我来使用视频目标分析工具，对视频前两秒进行帧级目标检测。\n\n","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{"finish_reason":"tool_calls","model_name":"qwen3.6-35b-a3b","model_provider":"openai"},"type":"ai","name":null,"id":"lc_run--019f892b-c31f-7022-b267-e0db98aefd0c","tool_calls":[{"name":"video_object_analytics","args":{"video_path":"/mnt/datasets/Vedio-demo/Trafic.mp4","operation":"detect","capture_seconds":2,"interval_seconds":0.5},"id":"call_a254431eb0ba4ac6b817412e","type":"tool_call"}],"invalid_tool_calls":[],"usage_metadata":{"input_tokens":11129,"output_tokens":411,"total_tokens":11540,"input_token_details":{},"output_token_details":{"reasoning":306}}},{"content":"{\"skill\": \"video-object-analytics\", \"status\": \"failed\", \"error_code\": \"RuntimeError\", \"message\": \"video analytics command returned no result\"}","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"tool","name":"video_object_analytics","id":"7806402b-4dcc-4a5c-b680-48fcde543b7c","tool_call_id":"call_a254431eb0ba4ac6b817412e","artifact":null,"status":"success"}],"intent_context":{"intent":"task","original_query":"帮我看看 /mnt/datasets/Vedio-demo/Trafic.mp4 前两秒的画面里有几个人、几辆车和其他主要目标。","normalized_query":"帮我看看 /mnt/datasets/vedio demo/trafic.mp4 前两秒的画面里有几个人、几辆车和其他主要目标。","routing_query":"场景：交通流量。场景ID：road_traffic。场景说明：道路交通流量、车流量、人流量、拥堵、速度、路口通行、OD、峰谷变化和交通运行态势分析场景。需要识别参数：分析区域、时间范围、指标、分析目标。用户原始问题：我需要对视频/mnt/datasets/Vedio-demo/Trafic.mp4的前两秒画面进行目标识别，并统计其中人、车辆及其他主要目标的数量","scene":"road_traffic","scene_name":"交通流量","params":{"时间范围":"前两秒","指标":"人、车及其他主要目标数量","分析目标":"目标识别"},"scene_mode":"single","scenes":["road_traffic"],"task_spans":[{"task_span_id":"span_a1083a","text":"帮我看看 /mnt/datasets/Vedio-demo/Trafic.mp4 前两秒的画面里有几个人、几辆车和其他主要目标。"}],"planning_steps":[{"task_span_id":"span_783c9d","text":"读取视频文件 /mnt/datasets/Vedio-demo/Trafic.mp4，定位并截取时间范围为前2秒的视频片段，执行帧解码与均匀采样，提取用于视觉分析的图像序列。预期产出：结构化存储的0-2秒视频帧数据集。"},{"task_span_id":"span_c013e2","text":"依托交通流量（road_traffic）场景的计算机视觉能力，调用目标检测算法对采样帧进行推理识别，按类别划分行人、各类车辆及其他交通主要目标，输出带边界框的目标检测结果列表。预期产出：包含目标类别、空间坐标及置信度的逐帧检测数据。"},{"task_span_id":"span_18323e","text":"针对“人、车及其他主要目标数量”指标，结合前两秒画面的时序连续性设定计数口径（如单帧快照统计或跨帧实体去重），对检测结果进行聚合计算。预期产出：各目标类别的量化统计结果及对应判定依据。"},{"task_span_id":"span_d3fcc8","text":"整合阶段统计结果，按任务要求格式化输出目标数量清单，明确标注分析的时间窗口、场景类型与数据来源，完成最终数据交付。预期产出：结构化目标计数报告。"}],"scene_tasks":[{"sub_task_id":"sub_ca2aee","scene":"road_t